# Everything under e2e/fixtures is generated by gen-fixtures.sh, up.sh, and
# write-kubeconfig.sh. Nothing in it is authored, so the whole tree is ignored
# rather than each kind of file in it: adding a fixture should not require a new
# rule here, and a rule per file is a rule someone forgets.
#
# What lands there is a P-384 private key, two copies of a shared HMAC secret,
# the API server's authentication configuration, and kubeconfigs holding cluster
# credentials. They are demo values, regenerated on demand and worthless to
# anyone. They are also exactly the shape of thing that must never reach a
# commit, and a scanner cannot tell the difference.
e2e/fixtures/

# The repository root ignores *~ but not vim's swap files, and this directory has
# collected a few.
.*.sw[a-z]
